; The identity element is what absorbs a difference of ARITY. Book chapter 13.
;
; Order and repetition are absorbed by :assoc-comm and :idempotent. Neither of
; those can align a 3-conjunct requirement against a 2-conjunct one: no
; reordering makes those the same shape. A declared unit can, by pairing the
; absent conjunct against the unit itself.
;
; The two halves below are the same two terms under signatures that differ in
; exactly one attribute. `AndU` has `:identity (Lit true)`; `AndN` does not.
; Everything else, including :assoc-comm-idem, is shared.

(sort Formula)
(sort Bucket)
(sort Region)

(function Lit (bool) Formula)
(function AndU (Formula) Formula :assoc-comm-idem :identity (Lit true))
(function AndN (Formula) Formula :assoc-comm-idem)

(function src () Bucket)
(function dst () Bucket)
(function regionOf (Bucket) Region)
(function versioningOn (Bucket) Formula)
(function encrypted (Bucket) Formula)
(function approvedRegion (Region) Formula)

; ── with the unit ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; Two conjuncts are reported as agreed and the dropped one is paired against
; `(Lit true)`, which is the report a reviewer needs: "both candidates require
; versioning and encryption; one additionally requires an approved region".
(let fullU
  (AndU
    (versioningOn (src))
    (encrypted (src))
    (approvedRegion (regionOf (dst)))))
(let droppedU
  (AndU
    (versioningOn (src))
    (encrypted (src))))
(antiunify fullU droppedU :algorithm exact)
(checkau fullU droppedU :max_size 10 :algorithm exact)

; ── without the unit ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
; One Variants node holding both conjunctions whole: size 13, and `:cr 1.0000`,
; which is the no-sharing endpoint of the compression ratio exactly. Nothing is
; reported as agreed even though two of the three conjuncts are identical.
(let fullN
  (AndN
    (versioningOn (src))
    (encrypted (src))
    (approvedRegion (regionOf (dst)))))
(let droppedN
  (AndN
    (versioningOn (src))
    (encrypted (src))))
(antiunify fullN droppedN :algorithm exact)
; `checkau` bounds the size from above only, so this states the size rather
; than asserting the gap: a result of size 10 would also satisfy it. The bound
; that carries the contrast is the `:max_size 10` above, which fails if the
; unit ever stops absorbing the arity difference.
(checkau fullN droppedN :max_size 13 :algorithm exact)
